      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-13T03:17:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, should have asked this right away:  what does CCD_BLOCK_EC_UART do? Can it be used for the purpose of this patch?",
      "parentUuid": "ce2fbc4d_3a852b56",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 509,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 509,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "a8574e2bba2129e9c96094c4bfcadbea60480e48",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "63588455_eb00d873",
        "filename": "board/cr50/rdd.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 509,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-13T16:30:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "CCD_BLOCK_EC_UART blocks the CCD EC UART output. It should not block packet mode, because that would prevent the EC from verifying RW and it could prevent the device from booting. It\u0027s mostly used to prevent cr50 from interfering with servo ec uart in test situations. They don\u0027t want to have to worry about interfering with packet mode.",
      "parentUuid": "89e33a9e_67c50db9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 509,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 509,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "a8574e2bba2129e9c96094c4bfcadbea60480e48",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dfeced05_f7fd64df",
        "filename": "board/cr50/rdd.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 509,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-13T16:59:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "could EC be tristated if both BLOCK_EC_UART and BLOCK_EC_CR50_COMM are enabled?\n\nI just find it confusing having three knobs for the same interface.",
      "parentUuid": "63588455_eb00d873",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 509,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 509,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "a8574e2bba2129e9c96094c4bfcadbea60480e48",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ef61832d_b41896b3",
        "filename": "board/cr50/rdd.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 509,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-13T17:44:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "CCD_BLOCK_EC_UART is for ec uart\nBLOCK_EC_CR50_COMM is for packet mode \nand \nTRISTATE_EC is a flag for the pulldown.\n\nIt\u0027s three flags for the same interface, but they control three things.\n\nIf we combine the flags, we\u0027ll have to do some stuff like \nGWRITE_FIELD(PINMUX, DIOB5_CTL, PD,\n\t\t\t     !!(ccd_block ^ (CCD_BLOCK_EC_UART | CCD_BLOCK_EC_CR50_COM));\n\t\t\t     \n\t\t\t   \nI think having a separate flag for the pulldown is more intuitive. The name TRISTATE_EC just explains why we\u0027re disabling all of this EC stuff with ccdblock TRISTATE_EC.",
      "parentUuid": "dfeced05_f7fd64df",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 509,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 509,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "a8574e2bba2129e9c96094c4bfcadbea60480e48",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dd50ab21_ef4ccea2",
        "filename": "board/cr50/rdd.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 509,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-13T18:24:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tend to see it as an additional confusion for the end user who would need to understand the difference between \u0027disable EC UART\u0027 and \u0027tristate EC UART\", and they do\u0027t really care.\n\nIf we did not add another option the check for pulldown would  be\n\nccd_block \u0026 (CCD_BLOCK_EC_UART | CCD_BLOCK_EC_CR50_COM) \u003d\u003d (CCD_BLOCK_EC_UART | CCD_BLOCK_EC_CR50_COM)\n\ni.e. do not add it if both bits are set.\n\nThis way we\u0027d add less code and achieve the same goal.",
      "parentUuid": "ef61832d_b41896b3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 509,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 509,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "a8574e2bba2129e9c96094c4bfcadbea60480e48",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2708b858_a3361c7c",
        "filename": "board/cr50/rdd.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 509,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-13T18:40:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this will require significant modifications to how uart tx is enabled in ccd_update_state, because we will need to start checking CCD_BLOCK_EC_CR50_COM. I guess we could separate enabling the pulldown from disabling ec uart tx.\n\nIt\u0027s easier to have three separate flags.\n\nI think it makes sense if you tristate the ec uart, then the outputs, EC comm and ec uart, will be disabled.\n\nI can rename the flag to CCDBLOCK_EC_UART_PD and make the user set these three flags independently.",
      "parentUuid": "dd50ab21_ef4ccea2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 509,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 509,
        "endChar": 38
